@ref Third Schedule item 5 (src:5643-5696)
DECLARE `sch 3 item 5 Purpose of the calculation` IS ONE OF
    `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)`
    `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)`
    `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case`

-- The weeks that item 5 averages over.  Each paragraph of the definition looks at its own weeks: paragraph (a) at the 3
-- weeks immediately preceding the termination of the contract or, where the employee was in employment for less than 3
-- weeks, at the first 3 weeks of employment; paragraph (b) at the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of absence or
-- period of absence or, for less than 3 weeks, the 3 weeks immediately following it; paragraph (c) at the 3 weeks
-- immediately preceding the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave or, for less than 3 weeks, the 3 weeks
-- immediately following it.  One list per limb, so that item 6 (paragraphs (a) and (b) "are not applicable in the third
-- column") reads a different list from item 5(a) and (b).
@ref Third Schedule item 5 (src:5643-5696)
DECLARE `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average` HAS
    `the purpose of the calculation` IS A `sch 3 item 5 Purpose of the calculation`
    `the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the termination of the contract` IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
    `the first 3 weeks of the employee's employment` IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
    `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of absence or period of absence` IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
    `the 3 weeks immediately following the day of absence or period of absence` IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
    `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
    `the 3 weeks immediately following the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`

-- Everything the Third Schedule needs to know about the employee's pay.  One record, so that a caller
-- (s 11, s 20A, s 28, s 37, s 38, s 76, s 87A, s 88, s 88A, s 89, each through s 107A) passes one thing.
-- src:5554 | 1. Where an The gross rate of pay for one day is to be The basic rate of pay for one day is to be
-- src:5555 | employee is calculated by dividing the total salary calculated by dividing the total salary
-- src:5556 | employed on including allowances but excluding — including wage adjustments and increments
-- src:5557 | piece rates. but excluding —
-- src:5641 | weeks.
@ref Third Schedule items 1 to 4 (src:5554-5641)
DECLARE `sch 3 Facts about the pay` HAS
    `the arrangement of pay` IS A `sch 3 Arrangement of pay`
    `the pay earned in the 14 days before the event` IS A `Pay for a period`
    `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days` IS A NUMBER
    `the monthly pay` IS A `Pay for a period`
    `the days required in the first week` IS A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
    `the days required in the second week` IS A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
    `the weeks for the average` IS A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
    `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- src:5709 | 7. In calculating the number of working days in a week or the average number of
-- src:5710 | working days in a week, any day on which an employee is required to work for
-- src:5711 | 5 hours or less under his or her contract of service is to be regarded as half a day.
@ref Third Schedule item 7 (src:5709-5711)
GIVEN week IS A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` MEANS
    week's `days required to work for more than 5 hours` PLUS (week's `days required to work for 5 hours or less` DIVIDED BY 2)

-- src:5698 | “week” means a continuous period of 7 days commencing at midnight on
-- src:5699 | Sunday.
@ref Third Schedule item 5 "week" (src:5698-5699)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 item 5 "week" the period is a week` MEANS
    IF (`the number of days in the period` EQUALS 7) AND `is a Sunday` `the first day of the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“week” means a continuous period of 7 days commencing at midnight on Sunday"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The average of the working days over a period of 3 weeks (item 7 applied to each week).
-- src:5643 | 5. In this Schedule —
-- src:5645 | “average number of working days in a week” means —
-- src:5647 | (a) for the purposes of calculating, under section 11(1), the salary
-- src:5648 | that is payable in lieu of notice of termination —
-- src:5650 | (i) the average number of days on which the employee
-- src:5651 | was required, under his or her contract of service, to
@ref Third Schedule item 5 (src:5643-5651)
GIVEN weeks IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` MEANS
    IF count weeks EQUALS 3
    THEN JUST (sum (map (GIVEN w YIELD `sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` w) weeks) DIVIDED BY 3)
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): every limb of item 5 averages "over the period of 3 weeks"; a list of any other length is not that period
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Paragraph (a): the salary payable in lieu of notice under s 11(1).
-- src:5647 | (a) for the purposes of calculating, under section 11(1), the salary
-- src:5648 | that is payable in lieu of notice of termination —
-- src:5650 | (i) the average number of days on which the employee
-- src:5651 | was required, under his or her contract of service, to
-- src:5656 | THIRD SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:5658 | work in a week over the period of 3 weeks immediately
-- src:5659 | preceding the termination of the contract; or
-- src:5661 | (ii) where the employee was in employment for less than
-- src:5662 | 3 weeks, the average number of days on which the
-- src:5663 | employee would have been required to work in a week
-- src:5664 | over the first 3 weeks of his or her employment, if the
-- src:5665 | contract of service had not been terminated;
@ref Third Schedule item 5(a) (src:5647-5665)
GIVEN weeks IS A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 item 5(a) the average number of working days in a week` MEANS
    IF weeks's `the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks`
    THEN `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (weeks's `the first 3 weeks of the employee's employment`)
    ELSE `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (weeks's `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the termination of the contract`)

-- Paragraph (b): the salary that may be deducted for absence under s 28(2).
