-- src:5680 | immediately following the day of absence or period of
-- src:5681 | absence, as the case may be;
@ref Third Schedule item 5(b) (src:5667-5681)
GIVEN weeks IS A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 item 5(b) the average number of working days in a week` MEANS
    IF weeks's `the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks`
    THEN `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (weeks's `the 3 weeks immediately following the day of absence or period of absence`)
    ELSE `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (weeks's `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of absence or period of absence`)

-- Paragraph (c): any other case.
-- src:5683 | (c) in any other case —
-- src:5685 | (i) the average number of days on which the employee
-- src:5686 | was required, under his or her contract of service, to
-- src:5687 | work in a week over the period of 3 weeks immediately
-- src:5688 | preceding the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period
-- src:5689 | of leave, as the case may be; or
-- src:5691 | (ii) where the employee was in employment for less than
-- src:5692 | 3 weeks, the average number of days on which the
-- src:5693 | employee was required to work under his or her
-- src:5694 | contract of service in a week over the period of 3 weeks
-- src:5695 | immediately following the rest day, holiday, day of
-- src:5696 | leave or period of leave, as the case may be;
@ref Third Schedule item 5(c) (src:5683-5696)
GIVEN weeks IS A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 item 5(c) the average number of working days in a week` MEANS
    IF weeks's `the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks`
    THEN `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (weeks's `the 3 weeks immediately following the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave`)
    ELSE `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (weeks's `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave`)

-- Item 5 as one rule: the paragraph that applies is the one for the purpose of the calculation.
-- src:5643 | 5. In this Schedule —
-- src:5645 | “average number of working days in a week” means —
-- src:5696 | leave or period of leave, as the case may be;
@ref Third Schedule item 5 (src:5643-5696)
GIVEN weeks IS A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` MEANS
    CONSIDER weeks's `the purpose of the calculation`
    WHEN `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` THEN `sch 3 item 5(a) the average number of working days in a week` weeks
    WHEN `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` THEN `sch 3 item 5(b) the average number of working days in a week` weeks
    WHEN `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` THEN `sch 3 item 5(c) the average number of working days in a week` weeks

-- Item 6: in the third column (the basic rate) paragraphs (a) and (b) are not applicable, so paragraph (c) applies
-- whatever the purpose: this reads the weeks of paragraph (c) and never those of paragraph (a) or (b).
-- src:5701 | 6. Paragraphs (a) and (b) of the definition of “average number of working days
-- src:5702 | in a week” in item 5 are not applicable in the third column.
@ref Third Schedule item 6 (src:5701-5702)
GIVEN weeks IS A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 item 6 the average number of working days in a week for the third column` MEANS
    `sch 3 item 5(c) the average number of working days in a week` weeks

-- The "total salary" of item 1, second column (gross rate): "total salary including allowances but excluding"
-- (a) overtime, (b) bonus or annual wage supplements, (c) reimbursement of special expenses, (d) productivity
-- incentive payments, (e) travelling, food and housing allowances.  "Salary" is the s 2(1) definition, which
-- already leaves out travelling allowances and reimbursements of special expenses, so those two are not taken
-- out a second time (fork F13).
