@ref Third Schedule item 1, second column (src:5554-5574)
GIVEN pay IS A `Pay for a period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3 item 1 the total salary for the gross rate of pay` MEANS
    `s 2(1) "salary" the amount` pay
        MINUS pay's `overtime payments`
        MINUS pay's `bonus payments or annual wage supplements`
        MINUS pay's `productivity incentive payments`
        MINUS pay's `food allowances`
        MINUS pay's `housing allowances`

-- Item 1, third column (basic rate): "total salary including wage adjustments and increments but excluding"
-- (a) overtime, (b) bonus or annual wage supplements, (c) reimbursement, (d) productivity incentive payments,
-- (e) any allowance however described.
@ref Third Schedule item 1, third column (src:5554-5574)
GIVEN pay IS A `Pay for a period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 3 item 1 the total salary for the basic rate of pay` MEANS
    `s 2(1) "salary" the amount` pay
        MINUS pay's `overtime payments`
        MINUS pay's `bonus payments or annual wage supplements`
        MINUS pay's `productivity incentive payments`
        MINUS pay's `food allowances`
        MINUS pay's `housing allowances`
        MINUS pay's `allowances of any other kind`

-- The formula of items 2, 3 and 4: 12 x the monthly rate of pay, over 52 x the days (or the average of the days).
-- src:5584 | The gross rate of pay for one day is to be
-- src:5585 | calculated according to the following 12 � monthly basic rate of pay
-- src:5586 | formula: 52 � number of days on which the
-- src:5587 | employee is required to work in a week:
-- src:5588 | 12 � monthly gross rate of pay
-- src:5589 | 52 � number of days on which the
-- src:5590 | employee is required to work in a week:
@ref Third Schedule items 2 to 4, the formula (src:5584-5590)
GIVEN `the monthly rate of pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days or the average number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` MEANS
    IF `the number of days or the average number of days` EQUALS 0
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the formula divides by 52 times the days the employee is required to work in a week; with none there is no quotient
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((12 TIMES `the monthly rate of pay`) DIVIDED BY (52 TIMES `the number of days or the average number of days`))

-- The gross rate of pay for one day (second column of the table).
-- src:5554 | 1. Where an The gross rate of pay for one day is to be The basic rate of pay for one day is to be
-- src:5555 | employee is calculated by dividing the total salary calculated by dividing the total salary
-- src:5556 | employed on including allowances but excluding — including wage adjustments and increments
-- src:5557 | piece rates. but excluding —
-- src:5584 | The gross rate of pay for one day is to be
-- src:5585 | calculated according to the following 12 � monthly basic rate of pay
-- src:5586 | formula: 52 � number of days on which the
-- src:5587 | employee is required to work in a week:
-- src:5588 | 12 � monthly gross rate of pay
-- src:5589 | 52 � number of days on which the
-- src:5590 | employee is required to work in a week:
-- src:5641 | weeks.
@ref Third Schedule items 1 to 4, second column (src:5554-5641)
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 3 Facts about the pay`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the arrangement of pay`
    WHEN `sch 3 item 1 piece rates` THEN
        -- item 1: the total salary earned in the 14 days divided by the number of days actually worked in them
        IF facts's `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days` EQUALS 0
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): item 1 divides "by the number of days on which the employee actually worked"; with none worked there is no quotient
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`sch 3 item 1 the total salary for the gross rate of pay` (facts's `the pay earned in the 14 days before the event`) DIVIDED BY facts's `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days`)
    WHEN `sch 3 item 2 monthly rate, the same number of days in every week` THEN
        -- item 2: 12 x monthly gross rate of pay / (52 x number of days the employee is required to work in a week)
        `sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` (`s 2(1) "gross rate of pay" the amount` (facts's `the monthly pay`)) (`sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (facts's `the days required in the first week`))
    WHEN `sch 3 item 3 monthly rate, a certain number of days in one week and a different number in the following week, in every period of 2 consecutive weeks` THEN
        -- item 3: 12 x monthly gross rate of pay / (52 x average number of days required to work in a week over any period of 2 consecutive weeks)
        `sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` (`s 2(1) "gross rate of pay" the amount` (facts's `the monthly pay`)) (((`sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (facts's `the days required in the first week`)) PLUS (`sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (facts's `the days required in the second week`))) DIVIDED BY 2)
    WHEN `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks` THEN
        -- item 4: the formula 12 x monthly gross rate of pay / (52 x average number of working days in a week), or "such other formula as the Commissioner may approve"
        CONSIDER facts's `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved`
        WHEN JUST approved THEN JUST approved
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (facts's `the weeks for the average`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST average THEN `sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` (`s 2(1) "gross rate of pay" the amount` (facts's `the monthly pay`)) average
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Third Schedule is for an employee on a monthly rate or on piece rates (s 107A); for an hourly, daily or weekly rate it states no calculation
    WHEN `sch 3 an arrangement the Third Schedule does not list` THEN NOTHING

-- The basic rate of pay for one day (third column of the table).
-- src:5554 | 1. Where an The gross rate of pay for one day is to be The basic rate of pay for one day is to be
-- src:5555 | employee is calculated by dividing the total salary calculated by dividing the total salary
-- src:5556 | employed on including allowances but excluding — including wage adjustments and increments
-- src:5557 | piece rates. but excluding —
-- src:5584 | The gross rate of pay for one day is to be
-- src:5585 | calculated according to the following 12 � monthly basic rate of pay
-- src:5586 | formula: 52 � number of days on which the
-- src:5587 | employee is required to work in a week:
-- src:5588 | 12 � monthly gross rate of pay
-- src:5589 | 52 � number of days on which the
-- src:5590 | employee is required to work in a week:
-- src:5641 | weeks.
@ref Third Schedule items 1 to 4, third column (src:5554-5641)
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 3 Facts about the pay`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the arrangement of pay`
    WHEN `sch 3 item 1 piece rates` THEN
        IF facts's `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days` EQUALS 0
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): item 1 divides "by the number of days on which the employee actually worked"; with none worked there is no quotient
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`sch 3 item 1 the total salary for the basic rate of pay` (facts's `the pay earned in the 14 days before the event`) DIVIDED BY facts's `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days`)
    WHEN `sch 3 item 2 monthly rate, the same number of days in every week` THEN
        `sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` (`s 2(1) "basic rate of pay" the amount` (facts's `the monthly pay`)) (`sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (facts's `the days required in the first week`))
    WHEN `sch 3 item 3 monthly rate, a certain number of days in one week and a different number in the following week, in every period of 2 consecutive weeks` THEN
        `sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` (`s 2(1) "basic rate of pay" the amount` (facts's `the monthly pay`)) (((`sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (facts's `the days required in the first week`)) PLUS (`sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (facts's `the days required in the second week`))) DIVIDED BY 2)
    WHEN `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks` THEN
        CONSIDER facts's `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved`
        WHEN JUST approved THEN JUST approved
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            -- item 6: in the third column only paragraph (c) of item 5 applies
            CONSIDER `sch 3 item 6 the average number of working days in a week for the third column` (facts's `the weeks for the average`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST average THEN `sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` (`s 2(1) "basic rate of pay" the amount` (facts's `the monthly pay`)) average
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Third Schedule is for an employee on a monthly rate or on piece rates (s 107A); for an hourly, daily or weekly rate it states no calculation
    WHEN `sch 3 an arrangement the Third Schedule does not list` THEN NOTHING

§ `Fourth Schedule -- Hourly basic rate of pay for overtime (s 38(6))`

-- The types of employee in the First column.  Item 3 is "[Deleted by Act 55 of 2018]" and has no constructor.
-- src:5715 | Section 38(6)
-- src:5717 | EMPLOYEE’S HOURLY BASIC RATE OF PAY FOR
-- src:5718 | CALCULATION OF PAYMENT DUE FOR OVERTIME
-- src:5720 | First column . Second column
-- src:5722 | Type of employee Calculation of hourly basic rate of pay
-- src:5724 | 1. A workman employed on a . 12 � monthly basic rate of pay
-- src:5725 | monthly rate of pay
-- src:5726 | 52 � 44
-- src:5728 | 2. A non-workman employed on a 12�monthly basic rate of pay
-- src:5729 | monthly basic rate of pay 52�44
-- src:5731 | 3. [Deleted by Act 55 of 2018]
-- src:5733 | 4. A workman employed on piece The total weekly pay at the basic rate
-- src:5734 | rates of pay received divided by the total
-- src:5735 | number of hours worked in the week
-- src:5737 | 5. A non-workman employed on The total weekly pay at the basic rate
-- src:5738 | piece rates of pay received divided by the total
-- src:5739 | number of hours worked in the week
-- src:5741 | 6. A workman employed on an Actual hourly basic rate of pay
-- src:5742 | hourly rate of pay
-- src:5744 | 7. A non-workman employed on an Actual hourly basic rate of pay
-- src:5745 | hourly rate of pay
-- src:5747 | 8. A workman employed on a daily Daily basic rate of pay divided by the
-- src:5749 | rate of pay number of working hours per day
-- src:5751 | 9. A non-workman employed on a Daily basic rate of pay divided by the
-- src:5752 | daily rate of pay number of working hours per day
@ref Fourth Schedule items 1 to 9 (src:5715-5752)
DECLARE `sch 4 Type of employee` IS ONE OF
    `sch 4 item 1 a workman employed on a monthly rate of pay`
    `sch 4 item 2 a non-workman employed on a monthly basic rate of pay`
    `sch 4 item 4 a workman employed on piece rates`
    `sch 4 item 5 a non-workman employed on piece rates`
    `sch 4 item 6 a workman employed on an hourly rate of pay`
    `sch 4 item 7 a non-workman employed on an hourly rate of pay`
    `sch 4 item 8 a workman employed on a daily rate of pay`
    `sch 4 item 9 a non-workman employed on a daily rate of pay`
    `sch 4 a type of employee that the First column does not list`

@ref Fourth Schedule items 1 to 9 (src:5715-5752)
DECLARE `sch 4 Facts about the pay` HAS
    `the type of employee` IS A `sch 4 Type of employee`
    `the monthly basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER
    `the total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received` IS A NUMBER
    `the total number of hours worked in the week` IS A NUMBER
    `the actual hourly basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER
    `the daily basic rate of pay` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of working hours per day` IS A NUMBER

@ref Fourth Schedule items 1 to 9 (src:5715-5752)
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 4 Facts about the pay`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the type of employee`
    -- items 1 and 2: 12 x monthly basic rate of pay / (52 x 44), whether the employee is a workman or not
    WHEN `sch 4 item 1 a workman employed on a monthly rate of pay` THEN JUST ((12 TIMES (facts's `the monthly basic rate of pay`)) DIVIDED BY (52 TIMES 44))
    WHEN `sch 4 item 2 a non-workman employed on a monthly basic rate of pay` THEN JUST ((12 TIMES (facts's `the monthly basic rate of pay`)) DIVIDED BY (52 TIMES 44))
    -- items 4 and 5: the total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received divided by the total number of hours worked in the week
    WHEN `sch 4 item 4 a workman employed on piece rates` THEN
        IF facts's `the total number of hours worked in the week` EQUALS 0
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): items 4 and 5 divide by "the total number of hours worked in the week"; with none worked there is no quotient
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (facts's `the total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received` DIVIDED BY facts's `the total number of hours worked in the week`)
    WHEN `sch 4 item 5 a non-workman employed on piece rates` THEN
        IF facts's `the total number of hours worked in the week` EQUALS 0
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): items 4 and 5 divide by "the total number of hours worked in the week"; with none worked there is no quotient
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (facts's `the total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received` DIVIDED BY facts's `the total number of hours worked in the week`)
    -- items 6 and 7: the actual hourly basic rate of pay
    WHEN `sch 4 item 6 a workman employed on an hourly rate of pay` THEN JUST (facts's `the actual hourly basic rate of pay`)
    WHEN `sch 4 item 7 a non-workman employed on an hourly rate of pay` THEN JUST (facts's `the actual hourly basic rate of pay`)
    -- items 8 and 9: the daily basic rate of pay divided by the number of working hours per day
    WHEN `sch 4 item 8 a workman employed on a daily rate of pay` THEN
        IF facts's `the number of working hours per day` EQUALS 0
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): items 8 and 9 divide by "the number of working hours per day"; with none there is no quotient
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (facts's `the daily basic rate of pay` DIVIDED BY facts's `the number of working hours per day`)
    WHEN `sch 4 item 9 a non-workman employed on a daily rate of pay` THEN
        IF facts's `the number of working hours per day` EQUALS 0
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): items 8 and 9 divide by "the number of working hours per day"; with none there is no quotient
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (facts's `the daily basic rate of pay` DIVIDED BY facts's `the number of working hours per day`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the First column lists types by their basis of pay and says nothing of an employee paid weekly or otherwise
    WHEN `sch 4 a type of employee that the First column does not list` THEN NOTHING

§ `Fifth Schedule -- Days of absence under s 76(1)(c)(ii)`

-- src:5819 | 7. In calculating the number of work days, any day on which a female employee
-- src:5820 | is required to work for 5 hours or shorter under her contract of service is to be
-- src:5821 | regarded as half a day.
@ref Fifth Schedule item 7 (src:5819-5821)
DECLARE `sch 5 Work days in a week` HAS
    `work days of more than 5 hours` IS A NUMBER
    `work days of 5 hours or shorter` IS A NUMBER

-- src:5778 | 1. Where the number of work . 4 × the number of work days in a week
-- src:5779 | days in a week is the same in
-- src:5780 | every week.
-- src:5782 | 2. Where the number of work 4 � the total number of work days
-- src:5783 | days varies from one week to in the number of fixed weeks
-- src:5784 | another and there is a The number of fixed weeks
-- src:5785 | consistent or regular pattern
-- src:5786 | repeated over a number of
-- src:5787 | fixed weeks.
-- src:5789 | 3. Where the number of work 4 × the average number of work days in a
-- src:5790 | days varies from one week to week over the period of 3 weeks
-- src:5791 | another and there is no immediately preceding the day of
-- src:5792 | consistent or regular pattern confinement or the first day of leave,
-- src:5793 | repeated over a number of whichever is the earlier
-- src:5794 | fixed weeks.
@ref Fifth Schedule items 1 to 3 (src:5778-5794)
DECLARE `sch 5 Work pattern` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 item 1 the number of work days is the same in every week`
    `sch 5 item 2 the number of work days varies and there is a consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks`
    `sch 5 item 3 the number of work days varies and there is no consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks`
    `sch 5 a pattern that none of items 1, 2 and 3 describes`

-- Everything the Fifth Schedule needs to know about the female employee's work pattern.
@ref Fifth Schedule items 1 to 3 (src:5778-5794)
DECLARE `sch 5 Facts about the work pattern` HAS
    `the work pattern` IS A `sch 5 Work pattern`
    `the work days in a week when the number is the same in every week` IS A `sch 5 Work days in a week`
    `the work days in each of the fixed weeks of the repeated pattern` IS A LIST OF `sch 5 Work days in a week`
    `the work days in each of the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of confinement or the first day of leave` IS A LIST OF `sch 5 Work days in a week`

-- src:5819 | 7. In calculating the number of work days, any day on which a female employee
-- src:5820 | is required to work for 5 hours or shorter under her contract of service is to be
-- src:5821 | regarded as half a day.
@ref Fifth Schedule item 7 (src:5819-5821)
GIVEN week IS A `sch 5 Work days in a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 item 7 the number of work days in the week` MEANS
    week's `work days of more than 5 hours` PLUS (week's `work days of 5 hours or shorter` DIVIDED BY 2)

-- src:5802 | 5. In this Schedule, where the number of days in the second column is not a
-- src:5803 | whole number, that number is to be rounded down to the nearest half day or
-- src:5804 | whole day.
@ref Fifth Schedule item 5 (src:5802-5804)
GIVEN number IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 item 5 the number rounded down to the nearest half day or whole day` MEANS
    (FLOOR (number TIMES 2)) DIVIDED BY 2

-- src:5796 | 4. In this Schedule, the calculation of the number of days on which a female
-- src:5797 | employee is entitled to absent herself from work under section 76(1)(c)(ii) is
-- src:5798 | to be determined in accordance with her work pattern under her contract of
-- src:5799 | service immediately preceding the day of confinement or the first day of
-- src:5800 | leave, whichever is the earlier.
@ref Fifth Schedule item 4 (src:5796-5800)
GIVEN `the day of confinement` IS A DATE
      `the first day of leave` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 5 item 4 the day by reference to which the work pattern is determined` MEANS
    IF `the day of confinement` AT MOST `the first day of leave`
    THEN `the day of confinement`
    ELSE `the first day of leave`

-- src:5806 | 6. In this Schedule —
-- src:5808 | “week” means a continuous period of 7 days commencing at midnight on
-- src:5809 | Sunday;
@ref Fifth Schedule item 6 "week" (src:5806-5809)
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 item 6 "week" the period is a week` MEANS
    IF (`the number of days in the period` EQUALS 7) AND `is a Sunday` `the first day of the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“week” means a continuous period of 7 days commencing at midnight on Sunday"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:5816 | “work pattern” means a work pattern described in item 1, 2 or 3 in the first
-- src:5817 | column.
@ref Fifth Schedule item 6 "work pattern" (src:5816-5817)
GIVEN pattern IS A `sch 5 Work pattern`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 item 6 "work pattern" the pattern is one` MEANS
    CONSIDER pattern
    WHEN `sch 5 item 1 the number of work days is the same in every week` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 item 2 the number of work days varies and there is a consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 5 item 3 the number of work days varies and there is no consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“work pattern” means a work pattern described in item 1, 2 or 3 in the first column"
    WHEN `sch 5 a pattern that none of items 1, 2 and 3 describes` THEN JUST FALSE

-- The number of days, before rounding, for the pattern the female employee has.
-- src:5778 | 1. Where the number of work . 4 × the number of work days in a week
-- src:5779 | days in a week is the same in
-- src:5780 | every week.
-- src:5782 | 2. Where the number of work 4 � the total number of work days
-- src:5783 | days varies from one week to in the number of fixed weeks
-- src:5784 | another and there is a The number of fixed weeks
-- src:5785 | consistent or regular pattern
-- src:5786 | repeated over a number of
-- src:5787 | fixed weeks.
-- src:5789 | 3. Where the number of work 4 × the average number of work days in a
-- src:5790 | days varies from one week to week over the period of 3 weeks
-- src:5791 | another and there is no immediately preceding the day of
-- src:5792 | consistent or regular pattern confinement or the first day of leave,
-- src:5793 | repeated over a number of whichever is the earlier
-- src:5794 | fixed weeks.
@ref Fifth Schedule items 1 to 3 (src:5778-5794)
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 5 Facts about the work pattern`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 items 1 to 3 the number of days before rounding` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the work pattern`
    -- item 1: 4 x the number of work days in a week
    WHEN `sch 5 item 1 the number of work days is the same in every week` THEN
        JUST (4 TIMES `sch 5 item 7 the number of work days in the week` (facts's `the work days in a week when the number is the same in every week`))
    -- item 2: 4 x the total number of work days in the number of fixed weeks, divided by the number of fixed weeks
    WHEN `sch 5 item 2 the number of work days varies and there is a consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` THEN
        IF null (facts's `the work days in each of the fixed weeks of the repeated pattern`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): item 2 divides by "the number of fixed weeks"; with no fixed week stated there is no quotient
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST ((4 TIMES sum (map (GIVEN w YIELD `sch 5 item 7 the number of work days in the week` w) (facts's `the work days in each of the fixed weeks of the repeated pattern`))) DIVIDED BY count (facts's `the work days in each of the fixed weeks of the repeated pattern`))
    -- item 3: 4 x the average number of work days in a week over the period of 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of confinement or the first day of leave, whichever is the earlier
    WHEN `sch 5 item 3 the number of work days varies and there is no consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` THEN
        IF count (facts's `the work days in each of the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of confinement or the first day of leave`) EQUALS 3
        THEN JUST ((4 TIMES sum (map (GIVEN w YIELD `sch 5 item 7 the number of work days in the week` w) (facts's `the work days in each of the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of confinement or the first day of leave`))) DIVIDED BY 3)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): item 3 averages "over the period of 3 weeks"; a list of any other length is not that period
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the three items describe a pattern the Schedule names; for any other pattern the Schedule states no calculation
    WHEN `sch 5 a pattern that none of items 1, 2 and 3 describes` THEN NOTHING

-- The number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself (S8).
-- src:5778 | 1. Where the number of work . 4 × the number of work days in a week
-- src:5779 | days in a week is the same in
-- src:5780 | every week.
-- src:5782 | 2. Where the number of work 4 � the total number of work days
-- src:5783 | days varies from one week to in the number of fixed weeks
-- src:5784 | another and there is a The number of fixed weeks
-- src:5785 | consistent or regular pattern
-- src:5786 | repeated over a number of
-- src:5787 | fixed weeks.
-- src:5789 | 3. Where the number of work 4 × the average number of work days in a
-- src:5790 | days varies from one week to week over the period of 3 weeks
-- src:5791 | another and there is no immediately preceding the day of
-- src:5792 | consistent or regular pattern confinement or the first day of leave,
-- src:5793 | repeated over a number of whichever is the earlier
-- src:5794 | fixed weeks.
-- src:5802 | 5. In this Schedule, where the number of days in the second column is not a
-- src:5803 | whole number, that number is to be rounded down to the nearest half day or
-- src:5804 | whole day.
@ref Fifth Schedule items 1 to 5 (src:5778-5804)
GIVEN facts IS A `sch 5 Facts about the work pattern`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 5 items 1 to 3 the number of days before rounding` facts
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST days THEN JUST (`sch 5 item 5 the number rounded down to the nearest half day or whole day` days)
